      "type": "narrative-update",
      "date": "2026-05-05T15:09:33.000Z",
      "title": "INDUSTOWER: Upcoming Results And Auditor Transition Will Drive Re Rating",
      "body": "Analysts have raised their price target on Indus Towers from ₹560 to ₹580, citing updated assumptions for the discount rate, revenue growth, profit margin and future P/E as the key drivers behind this change. What's in the News Board meeting scheduled for April 30, 2026, to consider and approve audited financial results for the fourth quarter and full financial year ended March 31, 2026 (company announcement).",
      "keyDevTypeId": null,
      "source_url": "https://simplywall.st/community/narratives/in/telecom/nse-industower/indus-towers-shares/lalu81ca-digital-india-and-5g-will-accelerate-network-densification-gains-jewt/updates/5-analysts-have-raised-their-price-target-on-indus-towers-from",
      "raw_subtype": "narrative-update"
    },
    {
      "id": "2315a9a8-4653-4815-9c7b-76115c289e5f",
      "type": "brief",
      "date": "2026-05-05T11:50:23.000Z",
      "title": "Full year 2026 earnings: Revenues and EPS in line with analyst expectations",
      "body": "Full year 2026 results: EPS: ₹27.09 (down from ₹37.31 in FY 2025). Revenue: ₹324.9b (up 7.9% from FY 2025). Net income: ₹71.4b (down 28% from FY 2025). Profit margin: 22% (down from 33% in FY 2025). The decrease in margin was driven by higher expenses. Revenue was in line with analyst estimates. Earnings per share (EPS) were also in line with analyst expectations. Revenue is forecast to grow 4.9% p.a. on average during the next 3 years, compared to a 3.6% growth forecast for the Telecom industry in Asia. Over the last 3 years on average, earnings per share has increased by 33% per year whereas the company’s share price has increased by 38% per year.",
      "keyDevTypeId": null,
      "source_url": null,
      "raw_subtype": "BriefActivity"
    },
    {
      "id": "1e1dc926-541d-4dd7-a7c3-1bea75af2b8a",
      "type": "brief",
      "date": "2026-05-04T17:05:49.000Z",
      "title": "New minor risk - Dividend sustainability",
      "body": "The company has an unstable dividend paying track record. The dividend has had an annual drop of over 20% in the past. Dividend yield: 3.5% This is considered a minor risk. If the company has cut or reduced its dividend in the past, it may be a sign that the underlying business is too cyclical to consistently maintain or grow the dividend over the long-term. It may also indicate the company prioritizes other outcomes instead of maintaining the dividend. For dividend paying companies, any reduction in the dividend can significantly impact the share price. Currently, the following risks have been identified for the company: Minor Risks Unstable dividend paying track record with dividend experiencing an annual drop of over 20% in the past. Profit margins are more than 30% lower than last year",
      "keyDevTypeId": null,
      "source_url": null,
      "raw_subtype": "BriefActivity"
    },
